  ('schladming-austria', '01F', 'Schladming', 'Austria', 'Four linked mountains, up to 760 km on one', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Austria', '{"ski","entertainment","family","adventure","wellness","culinary"}', '{"alpine","festive","dramatic"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["4-Berge-Skischaukel = Planai + Hochwurzen + Hauser Kaibling + Reiteralm, ~185 km piste (65.5 easy / 104.6 medium / 11.6 diff), 109 lift installations (brief''s ''123 km'' = legacy/marketing - use 185)","Ski amadé pass = up to ~760 km (356 pistes) across 25 places in 5 regions, ~270 lifts (Schladming-Dachstein is one member region)","Planai Nightrace = FIS World Cup night slalom (Planai a WC venue since 1973, night races since 1997); January; draws tens of thousands - the season''s wildest night","Hosted the FIS Alpine World Championships 2013 (and 1982)","Dachstein Glacier (Hoher Dachstein 2,995 m) nearby via Ramsau = year-round skiing + Skywalk/suspension bridge","Elevations ~728-2,015 m (Hauser Kaibling top ~2,015 m; Planai summit 1,894 m, base ~750 m); mid-altitude, heavy snowmaking (~90% coverage)","Village ~745 m, Styria (Steiermark), Liezen District, upper Ennstal; former mining town (~6,660 residents)","Reached by rail on the Ennstalbahn (Schladming''s own station; Bischofshofen-Selzthal) from Salzburg/Graz; airports Salzburg + Graz","Ski amadé pass standalone; no confirmed Ikon/Epic affiliation","Heli-skiing NOT available (Austria permits it only at Vorarlberg/Lech-Zurs sites)","Avalanche = Lawinenwarndienst STEIERMARK (Land Steiermark) via lawinen.report, EAWS 5-level - NOT SLF/Meteo, NOT Tirol/Vorarlberg","Wellness is hotel-spa-based; the public Erlebnistherme Amade is in Altenmarkt (Salzburg), NOT Schladming","Dense 4-star (+ some higher) hotel base, expanded for the 2013 Worlds (ratings to verify)","Nearest hospital = Schladming / Stainach-Rottenmann (LKH) area (verify)","A four-season town: winter 4-Berge + Nightrace, year-round Dachstein glacier, summer hiking/biking/events","Dachstein Skywalk + suspension bridge at Ramsau = a dramatic non-ski / summer high-country attraction","Rail-friendly: Schladming''s station was rebuilt barrier-free (island platform + underpass) for the 2013 Worlds"],"safety":{"emergency":"112 EU general / 140 Bergrettung alpine rescue / 144 ambulance / 133 police / 122 fire","hospital":"Schladming / Stainach-Rottenmann (LKH) area (verify); local practice for day cases; 140 Bergrettung / helicopter alpine evac","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"Mostly gentle pisted terrain but Schladminger Tauern off-piste + Dachstein glacier carry avalanche (+ crevasse) risk: Lawinenwarndienst STEIERMARK via lawinen.report, EAWS 5-level (NOT Tirol/Vorarlberg/SLF); transceiver/shovel/probe + guide off-piste, glacier roped-and-guided; Nightrace crowd safety; heli NOT available (Austria = Vorarlberg only); rescue 140 Bergrettung","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/austria","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:56Z","page_updated":"2026-08-11T10:19:06+01:00","source_country":"austria","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"High winter — Christmas/NY, Feb half-terms — and above all the Planai Nightrace (late January)","shoulder":"Early Dec opening + spring skiing; year-round Dachstein glacier covers the edges","green":"May-Jun + Oct-Nov (strong summer hiking/biking/events season; thinner winter crowds)","booking_lead":"Nightrace week + Christmas/NY + Feb 3-8 mo (Nightrace beds go far ahead); regular winter 2-4 mo","off_season_specials":"Year-round Dachstein glacier; summer hiking/biking + events; spring-ski value; 2013-Worlds legacy","event_peaks":"Planai Nightrace (late January), ski holidays (Dec-April), Christmas/NY; summer events","fire_date":"Nightrace + next winter by Aug-Sep; spring-ski from Jan; summer